# Language statistics
#
# GitHub's Linguist reports the whole repository by line count, which here reads as
# "mostly JavaScript" — accurate arithmetic, misleading answer. The shipped code is
# TypeScript and Rust; the JavaScript is the harness that proves it works.
#
# The tests are `.mjs` on purpose rather than by accident: they import from `dist/`, so
# they exercise the artifact that actually ships instead of the source that produced it.
# Rewriting them in TypeScript would mean either testing code that never ships, or
# adding a second compile step for tests. Neither is worth it — so the file below fixes
# the statistic instead of distorting the tests.
#
# Nothing here is excluded from CI, review, or the build. Only from the language bar.

# Throwaway experiments kept as the evidence behind DECISIONS.md D1 and D2. Not part of
# the project; not built, not shipped, not maintained.
spikes/**                       linguist-detectable=false

# Test suites and the harness around them.
packages/*/test/**              linguist-detectable=false
scripts/**                      linguist-detectable=false
conformance/*.mjs               linguist-detectable=false
bindings/node/conformance-adapter.mjs linguist-detectable=false

# The corpus is data, not source. Linguist would otherwise call it JSON.
conformance/vectors.json         linguist-generated=true

# Generated by tsc and cargo; never reviewed by hand.
**/dist/**                      linguist-generated=true
target/**                       linguist-generated=true
